#4
"Arghelan's Asylum"
"Dark depictions sketched along the stone walls give this otherwise stark room
an ominous feel.  A large fireplace is built into the southern wall, with dark
charcoal colored marble used as an edging around the opening as well as the
hearthstone.  A grand curved window extends outside the eastern wall of the
room, and a mat has been placed on the floor beside it for meditation and
prayer.  Carved into the center of the floor is some sort of symbol made up of
intertwining circles.  There is little in the way of furnishings to draw
attention from the cold gray stone in the room.  Thick furs and soft pelts
have been carefully placed upon the floor, providing the only comfortable
place to rest.  A few texts on fighting styles, philosophy and meditation have
been casually left around the room, open to passages recently read.  A large
stuffed bag made of a thick coarse fabric hangs by a chain from the ceiling in
the northwest corner of the room.  The only door to the room leads back out
into the hallway to the west.
"
""
