0 -1 23 0 6
E
"sketches"
"The walls of this room are covered in bleak scenes.  A sea of black and red,
one sketch flows into the next, creating a mural of hatred and pain.  One area
depicts a gruesome battle, the dead and dying covering the ground; another
shows some horrific types of torture being performed on what looks like an
elf.  Perhaps the most disturbing are some of the dark, sexual scenes, best
not studied too closely.  Cooled embers from the fireplace litter the floor
near the most recent sketch, some stained with dried blood.
"
E
"fireplace"
"This fireplace is built into the southern wall.  Dark, charcoal colored marble
edges the sides of the fireplace, giving it a more decorative look.  The
hearthstone comes out a few feet from the fireplace in a semi-circle, also
done in the charcoal colored marble.  An intense heat radiates from the fire
burning within the fireplace.  A few large logs have recently been placed over
the glowing embers.  Large flames are slowly beginning to lick the length of
the woods surface, causing light to flicker throughout the room.
"
E
"window"
"Centered in the eastern wall is a large semi-circular window.  The windowpanes
are curved slightly and extend beyond the wall, giving the window a large open
feel.  The window looks out over a large forested area, and possibly what
could be an old mine in the distance.  Given the direction the window faces,
it probably gives a spectacular view of the sunrise in the east.  A meditation
mat has been placed in the center of the semi-circle so that the window curves
around it on three sides.  Some dried white sandalwood rests in a small stone
bowl next to the mat, probably used to aid meditation.
"
E
"furs"
"Very little in this room could be called relaxing, but the thick bear skins,
piled on the floor look very inviting.  Adding to the look of comfort, brushed
lambskin has been rolled into pillows and mink and rabbit furs made into
oversized blankets.  This is the type of bed one could cuddle up in all day
and never think twice.  Although this looks very out of place in a room like
this, even the most dedicated have their vices, and guessing from the crimson
silk peeking out from under one of the blankets, this serves to support more
than one of them.
"
E
"training circle"
"Large intertwining circles are carved into the center of the stone floor.  An
oily reddish residue fills the deep grooves, which are also covered in dark
scorch marks.  The circles vary in size and position, but all join in the
center forming a small central circle.  This, one could assume, is meant to
signify the point where mind and body are one, and from there all else may be
realized.  The rings look to be used for training and conditioning of the body.
"
E
"texts"
"Various texts on fighting styles, philosophy and meditation litter the room. 
Old and new works alike seem to have been tossed aside once the reader had
finished with them.  One in particular though, sitting next to the fireplace,
catches your eye.  It is leather bound and looks to be open to a hand written
passage.
"
E
"passage"
"\"... But, in conclusion, I find I have insensibly reverted to the point I
desired; for, since it is now manifest to me that bodies themselves are not
properly perceived by the senses nor by the faculty of imagination, but by the
intellect alone; and since they are not perceived because they are seen and
touched, but only because they are understood [or rightly comprehended by
thought], I readily discover that there is nothing more easily or clearly
apprehended than my own mind.  But because it is difficult to rid one's self
so promptly of an opinion to which one has been long accustomed, it will be
desirable to tarry for some time at this stage, that, by long continued
meditation, I may more deeply impress upon my memory this new knowledge.\"
"
E
"down"
"No description.
"
