#6
"Nereus' Grotto of Inescapable Mortal Terror"
"Soft, white sand covers the floor of this cavernous grotto.  The walls have
been roughly chiseled out of solid marble; scratches from some sort of metal
tool are evident throughout the chamber.  A diffuse and pure white light fills
the room, illuminating the walls with a rippling, dancing light that moves in
time with the soft rhythm of the water.  It is almost as if a portion of the
ocean shallows has been pulled in its entirety and placed in this underground
cavern.  A sturdy metal chain gleams softly as the light of the room dances
with the water, attached to a large metal stake that has been driven into the
northern wall of the grotto.

In stark contrast to the peace of the scene, a number of gnawed bones have
been picked clean and are strewn across the northern side of the chamber.
"
"[Nereus] grue notes, where can a grue go?
