#29
"Quiet Pond"
"Pale light filters down from above to dance upon the small ripples on the
surface of this pond.  Silver-gleaming rushes rises abruptly from the banks;
the long grasses that grow upon the slopes bow gently to the force of the
kissing wind.  A sense of quietude lingers here, a peace and calmness found
nowhere else in the realm.  Even with the tranquillity, you sense a slight
energy that seems to begin under your very feet, a magic thrill that emanates
from the ground and whispers of creation and daydreams and stories from long
ago.  Out of place, but perhaps not entirely unexpected, you see a desk of
carved crystal atop the nearest bank, and upon it a single piece of paper. 
Behind the desk, almost as unlikely but still unsurprising, a sort of
chalkboard of glass and ivory stands, notes written upon its gleaming face.
"
""
